From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Subject: [PATCH 0035] meson-vdec: fix VP9 backward probability adaptation (the "four columns")

THIS is the owner's VP9 corruption: four vertical garbage columns on heavy
YouTube VP9. Upstream bug, present as of Linux 7.1.

In adapt_coef_probs() the binary mode/mv merge loop walks the count buffer two
counts at a time; an if/else-if chain maps the START of each count group to the
start of its probability group, and for every other position the running
coef_node_start must simply keep incrementing. The last branch was a bare
"else", which reset coef_node_start to VP9_MV_CLASS0_HP_0_START on EVERY
non-start position - so intra/inter, comp/single ref, tx and skip probabilities
were adapted into the wrong slots (the mv class0_hp ones) and the right slots
kept stale values.

Backward adaptation only happens when frame_parallel_decoding_mode = 0. Light
YouTube encodes use parallel mode (no adaptation) and decoded bit-exact; heavy
ones (e.g. psQ8Jfkhyp8 itag 248, peak 16 Mbit/s - the owner's class of stream)
do not. Frame 1 decodes from a context adapted after the KEY frame (coef only,
unaffected) and is right; frame 2 is the first to use a context adapted after
an INTER frame and is wrong, and the error rides every inter frame to the next
key frame. Each tile column's entropy decoding goes off the rails at its own
point: the capture hook's dump of frame 2 shows exactly four columns split at
x = 448 / 960 / 1408 (tile_cols_log2 = 2 read from the bitstream), correct at
the top, smooth prediction smear below.

Measured 23.09: dectest, 20 s of that stream, HW vs c2.android.vp9.decoder:
kernel #93 587/600 frames wrong, kernel #94 (this patch) 0/600 wrong in Y, U
and V. Live SmartTube on #95: 2457 frames, every one bit-exact to libvpx,
through 149 park/resume events and 10 seeks.

---
diff -ruN s34/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c s35/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
--- a/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/meson/vdec/codec_vp9.c
@@ -2105,7 +2105,19 @@
 			else if (coef_count_node_start ==
 					VP9_MV_BITS_1_COUNT_START)
 				coef_node_start = VP9_MV_BITS_1_START;
-			else /* node_start == VP9_MV_CLASS0_HP_0_COUNT_START */
+			/*
+			 * h96 0035 (23.09.2026): this was a bare "else" (upstream too,
+			 * as of Linux 7.1). Every count pair that is NOT the start of a
+			 * group must keep the running coef_node_start; the bare else
+			 * reset it to the MV class0_hp probabilities on every such pair,
+			 * so intra/inter, comp/single ref, tx and skip probabilities were
+			 * adapted into the wrong slots. Only streams with
+			 * frame_parallel_decoding_mode = 0 use backward adaptation, so
+			 * light YouTube VP9 was fine and heavy 1080p VP9 came out as four
+			 * garbage tile columns from the second inter frame on.
+			 */
+			else if (coef_count_node_start ==
+					VP9_MV_CLASS0_HP_0_COUNT_START)
 				coef_node_start = VP9_MV_CLASS0_HP_0_START;
 
 			den = count[coef_count_node_start] +
